  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Police Cooperation Liberia 2016 - 2019 - Policecooperation Liberia 2016 - 2019</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Polissamarbete Liberia 2016 - 2019</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Detta projekt syftar till att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra den liberianska polisens (LNP) kapacitet att utf&#xF6;ra grundl&#xE4;ggande brottsunders&#xF6;kningar, vilket inkluderar brottsplatsunders&#xF6;kning, bem&#xF6;tande av &#xF6;verlevare, vittnen och misst&#xE4;nkta, f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra samarbetet mellan polis och &#xE5;klagarmyndigheter i Liberia samt den specifika kapaciteten att utreda sexuellt och k&#xF6;nsrelaterat  v&#xE5;ld (SGBV).

Den svenska Polismyndigheten (SPA) kommer att arbeta f&#xF6;r att &#xF6;ka f&#xF6;rtroendet f&#xF6;r polisen och r&#xE4;ttsv&#xE4;sendet genom att st&#xE4;rka LNPs kapacitet inom utvalda omr&#xE5;den i Montserrado. SPA kommer att arbeta med kapacitetsuppbyggnad av LNP genom tr&#xE4;ningar och mentorskap. Fr&#xE4;mst kommer att SPA fokusera tr&#xE4;ningen p&#xE5; brottsplatsunders&#xF6;kning och uppgifterna f&#xF6;r den f&#xF6;rsta polisen som anl&#xE4;nder till en brottsplats och dennes f&#xF6;rm&#xE5;ga att skaffa korrekt och relevant information. Insatsen kommer ocks&#xE5; str&#xE4;va efter att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra samarbetet mellan polis och &#xE5;klagare och &#xF6;ka den &#xF6;msesidiga f&#xF6;rst&#xE5;elsen f&#xF6;r att kunna underl&#xE4;tta hanteringen av fallen i domstol. Detta &#xE4;r ett kritiskt omr&#xE5;de f&#xF6;r att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra det straffr&#xE4;ttsliga arbetet i Liberia. Insatsen syftar &#xE4;ven till att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra LNPs arbete med SGBV-fall.

Insatsen har &#xE4;ven som m&#xE5;l att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra dialogen mellan polis och samh&#xE4;lle. SPA avser d&#xE4;rf&#xF6;r arbeta med LNP kring hur de kommunicerar med allm&#xE4;nheten. Detta &#xE4;r s&#xE4;rskilt viktigt kopplat till SGBV fall, men &#xE4;ven i alla f&#xF6;rh&#xF6;r med misst&#xE4;nkta, vittnen och offer liksom i alla interaktioner med allm&#xE4;nheten. Detta &#xE4;r en viktig del av SPAs mentorskap av LNP. F&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttrad dialog och en f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttring i hur polisen behandlar medborgare &#xE4;r t&#xE4;nkt att &#xF6;ka f&#xF6;rtroendet i den formella r&#xE4;ttvise- och s&#xE4;kerhetssektorn. 

Denna insats kommer att begr&#xE4;nsas till tre utvalda omr&#xE5;den som kommer att fungera som pilotstationer. d&#xE4;r SPA vill f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra kapaciteten hos LNP i brottsunders&#xF6;kningar, f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra dialogen med medborgarna samt f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra samarbetet mellan polis och &#xE5;klagarv&#xE4;sendet. SPA kommer att ing&#xE5; i ett Memorandum of Understanding med LNP d&#xE4;r ansvarsf&#xF6;rdelning och formellt &#xE5;tagande till projektet bekr&#xE4;ftas. Sammantaget syftar detta till att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra de formella straffr&#xE4;ttsliga processerna och dess bidrag till konfliktl&#xF6;sning samt att &#xF6;ka medborgarnas tillg&#xE5;ng till r&#xE4;ttvisa.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve the capacity of the Liberian Police (LNP) to conduct basic criminal investigations, which includes crime scene investigations, treatment of survivors, witnesses and suspects, improving cooperation between police and prosecutors in Liberia and the specific capacity to investigate sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV). ).

The Swedish Police Authority (SPA) will work to increase confidence in the police and the judiciary by strengthening LNP&apos;s capacity in selected areas in Montserrado. SPA will work with capacity building of LNP through training and mentorship. The SPA will mainly focus the training on crime scene investigation and the information for the first police officer to arrive at a crime scene and his ability to obtain correct and relevant information. The effort will also strive to improve cooperation between the police and prosecutors and increase mutual understanding in order to facilitate the handling of cases in court. This is a critical area for improving criminal justice work in Liberia. The effort also aims to improve LNP&apos;s work with SGBV cases.

The effort also aims to improve the dialogue between the police and society. SPA therefore intends to work with LNP on how they communicate with the public. This is particularly important in connection with SGBV cases, but also in all interrogations with suspects, witnesses and victims as well as in all interactions with the public. This is an important part of SPA&apos;s mentorship of LNP. Improved dialogue and an improvement in how the police treat citizens are intended to increase confidence in the formal justice and security sector.

This effort will be limited to three selected areas that will serve as pilot stations. where the SPA wants to improve the capacity of the LNP in criminal investigations, improve the dialogue with citizens and improve cooperation between the police and the prosecution service. SPA will be part of a Memorandum of Understanding with LNP where the division of responsibilities and formal commitment to the project is confirmed. Overall, this aims to improve formal criminal justice processes and their contribution to conflict resolution, as well as to increase citizens&apos; access to justice.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of this intervention is to contribute to improved public trust in the Liberian National Police (LNP) through improved quality in crime investigations in the selected areas where the project is implemented.&#xA0;The project seeks to achieve improved quality of crime investigations including SGBV, basic crime scene investigation and enhanced cooperation betweeen the LNP and the Prosecution Service in three police station areas in Monrovia.</narrative>
  </description>
